course: dictionary
lesson: 10167
title: The tibia, your shinbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your lower leg has two long bones. The bigger and stronger one at the front is the tibia, also called the shinbone. It runs from your knee down to your ankle.
explain: «The shin bone, the tibia, lies just under the skin with little padding, which is why kicks hurt.» The clues are "just under the skin" and "little padding": there is not much to soften a blow, so the bone is easy to feel.
explain: The thin bone beside the tibia is the fibula. Together they carry most of your weight, which is why footballers wear shin guards to protect the tibia.
fact: The tibia is the shinbone, the bigger and stronger of the two bones in your lower leg.
fact: The tibia sits between your knee and your ankle.
fact: The tibia is named in science lessons with the femur (thigh bone), the fibula and the patella (kneecap).
fact: In insects, the tibia is one of the sections of the leg.
fact: A broken tibia means the shinbone has cracked or snapped.
exercise: «The shin bone, the tibia, lies just under the skin.» What is the tibia? | *The shinbone, the bigger bone in the lower leg | The kneecap | The thigh bone | A bone in the arm
exercise: Which thin bone runs beside the tibia? | The femur | *The fibula | The ankle | The patella
exercise: In an insect, what is the tibia? | The insect's wing | *One section of the insect's leg | The insect's head | The insect's eye
test: Why do footballers wear shin guards? | *To protect the tibia from kicks | For the team colours | To keep their legs warm | To make them run faster
test: Where does the tibia lie? | The hip and the knee | The shoulder and the elbow | *Between the knee and the ankle | Between the wrist and the fingers
exam: Which bone is the thigh bone, named with the tibia in science lessons? | *The femur | The tibia | The patella | The fibula
